## API Contract Summary

Your friend needs to know these endpoints to build the frontend:

### `POST /api/v1/triage`
```json
// Request
{ "symptoms": "string", "userId": "string" }

// Response
{
  "riskLevel": "Low | Moderate | High",
  "primaryRecommendation": "string",
  "possibleCategories": ["string"]
}
```

### `POST /api/v1/chat/audio`
```
// Request: multipart/form-data with audio blob
// Response
{
  "transcribedText": "string",
  "geminiResponse": "string",
  "audioBase64": "string"
}
```

### `GET /api/v1/insights`
```json
// Response
{ "tip": "string" }
```

### `GET /api/v1/encyclopedia/:query`
```json
// Response
{
  "disease": "string",
  "summary": "string",
  "symptoms": ["string"],
  "prevention": ["string"]
}
```

---

## Tech Stack Reference

| Component | Package | Version |
|-----------|---------|---------|
| Runtime | Node.js | 20+ |
| Framework | Express | ^4.21 |
| Language | TypeScript | ^5.x |
| AI | @google/generative-ai | ^0.21 |
| STT | vosk | ^0.3 |
| TTS | google-tts-api | ^2.0 |
| Database | @supabase/supabase-js | ^2.x |
| File Upload | multer | ^1.4 |
| CORS | cors | ^2.8 |
| Dev | tsx | ^4.x |
| Dev | nodemon | ^3.x |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The shared `api.types.ts` file is the **contract** between frontend and backend. Any changes here must be communicated to both developers.
